{"school":{"dbn":"30Q300","name":"The 30th Avenue School","boro":"Queens","district":"30","district_label":"District 30","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"K-8","grades":"K to 8","status":"open","enrollment":525,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"28-37 29 STREET, Queens, NY 11102","phone":"718-626-8502","website":"www.ps300q.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/64631","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"Q300 is a K-8 citywide gifted and talented school located in the heart of Astoria. Students at Q300 have many diverse talents, abilities and are always looking to learn more. Our mission is to graduate students who collaborate with others to ask meaningful questions, to solve complex problems, and to engage responsibly with their communities and beyond. In Middle school, our programming is designed to ensure students will succeed across all subject content areas and are supported social-emotionally throughout. Students will have access to advance classes such as Honors English, Honors Social Studies, Honors Science, which prepare them to take the Living Environment Regents in 8th grade, and Honors Math, which prepares them to take the Algebra I regents in 8th grade. In addition, students have the opportunity to engage in Computer Science Art, and Spanish Language at least twice a week. Extracurricular activities and teams include Debate team and Math Team. At Q300, we emphasis our core values of inclusion, inquiry, and responsibility to create a warm and welcoming environment for all.","start_time":"08:29am","end_time":"02:50pm","languages":null,"subway":"N, Q to 30 Av-Grand Av","bus":"M60-SBS, Q100, Q101, Q102, Q104, Q18, Q19, Q69","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":"Astoria","latitude":40.768181,"longitude":-73.922404,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.983],"st":["ok"],"n":[281.0]},"at